I've found the tilted terminal component. Here's a comprehensive report:

## 1. Full Paths of All Files Involved

- [docs/.vitepress/theme/components/GetStartedTabs.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/GetStartedTabs.vue) — Main 3D flip container and styling
- [docs/.vitepress/theme/components/TerminalChrome.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/TerminalChrome.vue) — Window chrome bar (traffic-light dots, play/pause button)
- [docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CommandCycleRow.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/CommandCycleRow.vue) — Typewriter text animation with cursor and copy button
- [docs/.vitepress/theme/components/useCommandCycle.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/useCommandCycle.ts) — Typing/deleting/hold cycle controller (reactive state machine)
- [docs/.vitepress/theme/get-started.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/get-started.ts) — Localized strings config

## 2. Complete CSS for the 3D Tilt

### Core 3D Perspective and Transform Setup
**File:** [GetStartedTabs.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/GetStartedTabs.vue#L383-L460)

```css
.gs-started__stage {
  position: relative;
  aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
  perspective: 1100px;
}
```

### Shadow Under the Tilted Card
```css
.gs-started__stage::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 0;
  inset-inline: 4%;
  inset-block-end: -48px;
  block-size: 22px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
  filter: blur(10px);
  pointer-events: none;
  transform: rotateY(-15deg);
  transition: transform 560ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
}

.gs-started__stage.-agent::after {
  transform: rotateY(165deg);
}

:dir(rtl) .gs-started__stage::after {
  transform: rotateY(15deg);
}

:dir(rtl) .gs-started__stage.-agent::after {
  transform: rotateY(-165deg);
}
```

### Main Flipper Container (Critical Firefox Hack)
```css
.gs-started__flipper {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 1;
  inset: 0;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;
  transform: rotateY(-15deg);
  transition: transform 560ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  /* Keeps the tilted bitmap on its own compositor layer so per-keystroke typewriter repaints
     don't force Firefox to re-rasterize it, which otherwise tears the tilted edges. */
  will-change: transform;
}

.gs-started__stage.-agent .gs-started__flipper {
  transform: rotateY(165deg);
}

:dir(rtl) .gs-started__flipper {
  transform: rotateY(15deg);
}

:dir(rtl) .gs-started__stage.-agent .gs-started__flipper {
  transform: rotateY(-165deg);
}
```

### Face Styling (Backface Hidden)
```css
.gs-started__face {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  backface-visibility: hidden;
  will-change: transform;
  background: light-dark(
    var(--instui-color-background-container),
    var(--instui-color-background-page)
  );
  border-radius: 8px;
}

.gs-started__face--agent {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
```

### Terminal Container (Another Compositor Layer)
```css
.gs-terminal {
  block-size: 100%;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  border: 1px solid var(--vp-c-divider);
  border-radius: 8px;
  background: light-dark(
    var(--instui-color-background-container),
    var(--instui-color-background-page)
  );
  /* Own compositor layer so interior repaints (copy button hover, popovers) don't re-rasterize
     the tilted face bitmap and tear its edges. */
  will-change: transform;
}
```

### Terminal Body
```css
.gs-terminal__body {
  flex: 1;
  min-block-size: 0;
  padding: 1.5rem;
  direction: ltr;
  text-align: start;
  /* Visible, not hidden: the copy button's "copied" popover sits above the command row and would
     otherwise get clipped right where it overlaps the chrome bar. */
  overflow: visible;
}

.gs-terminal__body pre {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  box-shadow: none;
  background: transparent;
  overflow: visible;
}

.gs-terminal__body code {
  border: 0;
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--instui-component-text-primary-color);
  font-family: var(--vp-font-family-mono, monospace);
}
```

### Agent Terminal Variant
```css
.gs-agent-terminal__body {
  padding: 0;
  /* Lets the AI-tool popover escape the chrome instead of being clipped by it. */
  overflow: visible;
}

.gs-agent__body {
  position: relative;
  padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
  /* Clips this gradient layer's own corners since ancestors no longer clip for us. */
  border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: linear-gradient(
    180deg,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--vp-c-bg-soft) 45%, transparent),
    transparent
  );
}

.gs-agent__input-wrap {
  position: relative;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-block-size: 0;
  direction: ltr;
  text-align: start;
  padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--vp-c-divider);
  background: light-dark(#ffffff, #11161c);
  border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px;
  font-family: var(--vp-font-family-mono, monospace);
}
```

## 3. Browser-Specific Hacks

**Firefox Compositor Layer Workaround** (lines 421-426, 433-439 in GetStartedTabs.vue):
- **Issue:** Per-keystroke typewriter animation causes Firefox to re-rasterize the tilted bitmap on every character, tearing the edges
- **Fix:** `will-change: transform` on both `.gs-started__flipper` and `.gs-terminal` to promote them to their own compositor layers, preventing costly rasterization on each keystroke
- **Why:** The tilted 3D transform combined with frequent DOM updates/repaints forces Firefox to continuously re-rasterize the tilted surface bitmap unless explicitly placed on an isolated layer

No `-moz-`, `@-moz-document`, or `@supports (-moz-appearance)` blocks found — the `will-change` property is the only Firefox-specific mitigation.

## 4. Terminal Content Type & Animation

**Content:** Plain text with colored inline elements
- **Type:** DOM text nodes (`<pre><code>` wrapping CommandCycleRow components)
- **NOT:** SVG, canvas, or image
- **Icon system:** InstUI icons rendered as CSS `.instui-icon.-icon-{name}` classes (simple-icons and custom icon sets)

**Animation Type:** Typewriter effect with character-by-character typing
- **Controller:** `useCommandCycle` composable ([lines 54-108](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/useCommandCycle.ts))
- **Phases:** idle → typing → paused → deleting → (repeat)
- **Timing:**
  - Type: 70ms per character (50ms for agent prompts)
  - Delete: 40ms per character (27ms for agent)
  - Hold (mid-cycle): 1400ms
  - Initial hold: 1700ms
  - Cursor blink: 600ms
- **Cursor:** Animated inline `<span class="gs-command-row__cursor">` with `0.3s step-end` blink animation
- **Copy feature:** Interactive popover showing package-manager options and a copy button that cycles through pm choices (vpx/pnpm/deno/bun/npm/yarn for CLI, claude/gemini/cursor/copilot/q for agents)

## 5. Masks, Clip-path, Gradients & Pseudo-Elements

### Gradients
Only one gradient in the tilted component:
- **Agent body gradient** (lines 557-559):
  ```css
  background: linear-gradient(
    180deg,
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--vp-c-bg-soft) 45%, transparent),
    transparent
  );
  ```
  This creates a subtle fade from semi-opaque to fully transparent; clipped to agent body corners due to `border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px; overflow: hidden`

### Pseudo-Elements
- **`.gs-started__stage::after`** — Shadow beneath the card, rotates with the flipper
- **`.gs-terminal__dot.-red`, `.-yellow`, `.-green`** (TerminalChrome.vue) — Traffic-light circles (no gradients, solid colors)

### Clip-path & Masks
**None found** on the tilted component itself. The comment at line 554 clarifies that `.gs-agent__body` clipping its own corners with `border-radius + overflow: hidden` is necessary because "ancestors no longer clip for us" (due to `overflow: visible` on parent `.gs-agent-shell`).

## 6. prefers-reduced-motion Handling

**File:** [GetStartedTabs.vue](docs/.vitepress/theme/components/GetStartedTabs.vue#L595-L598)

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .gs-started__flipper,
  .gs-started__stage::after {
    transition: none;
  }
}
```

**Behavioral layer** (TypeScript):
- Lines 136, 147: Detected at mount via `window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches`
- Line 137: Stored in reactive `reducedMotion` ref
- Line 133: Passed to `useCommandCycle` options
- When `reducedMotion.value === true`, the typing animation stops advancing character-by-character and jumps straight to the fully-typed state (no gradual typing)

**CommandCycleRow animation** (lines 314-316):
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .gs-command-row__cursor--blink {
    animation: none;
  }
}
```

The cursor blink animation is removed, though the cursor itself remains visible as a static `<span>`.

## 7. docs/engineering-log.md Entries

**Search for Firefox/3D/transform/antialiasing mentions:** No dedicated section for this component exists in engineering-log.md. The repository's engineering log covers:
- Security (SVG injection, CLI flag validation)
- Toolchain (oxfmt CSS corruption with tagged templates)

**But the Firefox behavior is documented inline** in the GetStartedTabs.vue CSS comments themselves (lines 422-424):
> "Keeps the tilted bitmap on its own compositor layer so per-keystroke typewriter repaints don't force Firefox to re-rasterize it, which otherwise tears the tilted edges."

This is a hard-won lesson embedded directly in the code rather than in the log—suggesting it was discovered during development and prioritized for inline documentation to prevent regression.

## Responsive Behavior

**Narrow viewports** (< 960px width):
```css
@media (max-width: 959px) {
  .gs-started {
    margin-block: 2rem;
  }

  .gs-started__flipper,
  .gs-started__stage::after {
    transform: rotateY(0deg);
  }

  .gs-started__stage.-agent .gs-started__flipper,
  .gs-started__stage.-agent::after {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }
}
```

On narrow screens, the 3D tilt is disabled (flattened to 0°/180° binary flip with no depth) because the perspective cannot be read as depth in the confined space.
